From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Projet AuxiNux <repo@auxinux.ca>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:14:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] shell: standard termination on SIGTERM (Linux)

When the event loop starts, the engine (desktop-sdk) installs a SIGTERM handler that closes the application from inside the signal handler; it ends in a segmentation fault, so every session logout produced a crash and a core dump. Once that handler is in place, restore the default action of SIGTERM (immediate termination, no core dump).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 win-linux/src/main.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/win-linux/src/main.cpp b/win-linux/src/main.cpp
index c9a03e3..4690ec4 100644
--- a/win-linux/src/main.cpp
+++ b/win-linux/src/main.cpp
@@ -193,6 +193,9 @@ int main( int argc, char *argv[] )
     AuxiNux::installTranslator();
 #endif
     application_cef->Init_CEF(&AscAppManager::getInstance(), argc, argv);
+#if defined(AUXI_PRODUCT_NAME) && defined(__linux)
+    AuxiNux::restoreDefaultSignals();
+#endif
     /* ********************** */
 
 //    GET_REGISTRY_SYSTEM(reg_system)
